## DESCRIPTION
## Evaluate the indefinite integral of x e^(ax) using integration by parts.
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## Tagged by cmd6a 8/9/06

## DBsubject(Calculus - single variable)
## DBchapter(Techniques of integration)
## DBsection(Integration by parts (without trigonometric functions))
## Date(8/23/07)
## Institution(Union College)
## Author(K. Lesh)
## MLT(notrig_01)
## MLTleader(1)
## Level(3)
## MO(1)
## KEYWORDS('calculus','integration','integration by parts')

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros(
    'PGstandard.pl',                'PGML.pl',
    'parserFormulaUpToConstant.pl', 'PGcourse.pl'
);

$a = random(2, 9);

$antiderivative = FormulaUpToConstant("e^($a x)/$a^2 * ($a x - 1) + C");

BEGIN_PGML
Evaluate the indefinite integral.

[``\int x e^{[$a]x} \, dx ={}``] [_]{$antiderivative}{35}
END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
Use integration by parts, [`\int u \, dv = uv - \int v \, du`],

[#
    [.with.]    [.[`u = x`].]   [.and.] [.[`dv = e^{[$a]x} \, dx`],.]*
    [.so that.] [.[`du = dx`].] [.and.] [.[`v = \frac{1}{[$a]} e^{[$a]x}`]..]
#]*

Then

[```
\begin{aligned}
\int x e^{[$a]x} \, dx
&= \frac{1}{[$a]} x e^{[$a]x} - \int \frac{1}{[$a]} e^{[$a]x} \, dx \\
&= \frac{1}{[$a]} x e^{[$a]x} - \frac{1}{[$a**2]} e^{[$a]x} + C \\
&= \frac{e^{[$a]x}}{[$a**2]} \left([$a]x - 1\right) + C.
\end{aligned}
```]
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();
